      "notes": "ROLLING SCHEDULE: do the next session in the cycle (Upper A → Lower A → Upper B → Lower B), whatever day it is. Missed a day? Just do the next one—never double up. Thursday stays a full rest day.\nSupersets: alternate the two moves back-to-back, then take the listed rest after the SECOND move (timers are set to that).\nEffort: 1–2 reps in reserve on compounds, 0–1 on the last set of isolations. Stop a set when form breaks.\nProgression: when every set hits the TOP of the range at ≤2 RIR, add 2.5–5 lb (one pin on cables) next time.\nTime cap: if the session runs past ~55 min, cut the last pair to 2 rounds instead of skipping it.\n\nSS A (2 min): leg press + calf raise (you've swapped hack squat for leg press every time, so it's now the default; hack squat is a swap if you want variety).\nSS B (75 sec): leg extension + seated leg curl.\nSS C (60 sec): cable crunch + hanging leg raise.\nFinish: 5–10 min easy incline walk (optional).\n~16 sets.",
